# 18 Boundary conditions on the domain {#ch:bc}

## Boundary conditions are ghost values

Basilisk never writes a special stencil for a boundary cell. Instead, before
a field is read near the boundary, it fills the ghost cells outside the
domain, and the ordinary interior stencil does the rest. A boundary
condition is a formula for the ghost value. In that formula, `s[]`
(written $s_i$ below) is the interior cell next to the boundary, and the
coordinates `x`, `y`, `z` are those of the boundary
*face*, the point halfway between the interior cell centre and the
ghost centre (figure 18.1).

